   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "יוֹשֵׁב מְנָלַן? אָמַר רָבָא אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן, אָמַר קְרָא: ״לַעֲמֹד לְשָׁרֵת״ – לַעֲמִידָה בְּחַרְתִּיו, וְלֹא לִישִׁיבָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that a priest who is «sitting» disqualifies the rites that he performs. The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive this? «Rava says» that «Rav Naḥman says: The verse states» with regard to the priests: “For the Lord your God has chosen him out of all your tribes, «to stand to minister”» (Deuteronomy 18:5). The verse indicates that «I have chosen him for standing and not for sitting.»"
  }
